---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Stellar Astrophysics Cheat Sheet | Free Stars, Spectra, Luminosity"
  description="Complete stellar astrophysics cheat sheet with stars, spectra, and luminosity. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Stellar Astrophysics<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Stars, spectra, and luminosity. From stellar properties to classification.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Stellar Properties</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Basic Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Luminosity: L = 4πR²σT⁴
Flux: F = L/(4πd²)
Color index: B - V (blue - visual)
Spectral type: O B A F G K M (hot to cool)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Magnitude System</h3>
        <pre><code>Apparent magnitude: m
Absolute magnitude: M
Distance modulus: m - M = 5 log(d/10)
Bolometric magnitude: M_bol</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>HR Diagram</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Diagram Features</h3>
        <pre><code>x-axis: Temperature (decreasing right)
y-axis: Luminosity (increasing up)
Main sequence: diagonal band
Red giants: cool, luminous
White dwarfs: hot, dim</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Stellar Classification</h3>
        <pre><code>O: T > 30,000 K, blue
B: 10,000-30,000 K, blue-white
A: 7,500-10,000 K, white
F: 6,000-7,500 K, yellow-white
G: 5,200-6,000 K, yellow (Sun)
K: 3,700-5,200 K, orange
M: < 3,700 K, red</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Stellar Structure</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Interior Model</h3>
        <pre><code>Core: nuclear fusion
Radiative zone: energy transported by photons
Convective zone: energy transported by convection
Photosphere: visible surface
Chromosphere: thin outer layer
Corona: extended atmosphere</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Stellar Atmospheres</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Spectral Lines</h3>
        <pre><code>Absorption lines: cooler gas absorbs photons
Emission lines: hot gas emits photons
Fraunhofer lines: solar absorption lines
Doppler shift: radial velocity measurement
Stark effect: pressure broadening</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
